quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  10,89,"He said: ‘(O Moses and Aaron!) Your supplication has been answered. So remain steadfast, and do not follow the way of those who do not know.’"
  10,90,"And We carried the Children of Israel across the sea. Then, Pharaoh and his troops pursued them out of defiance and aggression. But when drowning overtook him, he called out: ‘I believe there is no god except the One in whom the Children of Israel have believed. And I am among those who submit (to Him).’"
  10,91,(He was told:) ‘What! Now? But you have always disobeyed before. And you were among the corruptors!
  10,92,"So today, We shall save (only) your corpse so that you may be a sign for those who come after you. Indeed, the majority of the people are negligent of Our signs.’"
  10,93,"Indeed, We settled the Children of Israel in a worthy place and provided good things as sustenance for them. And they did not differ until the knowledge (of the Torah) came to them. Your Lord will indeed judge between them on the Day of Resurrection concerning what they used to differ."
  10,94,"(O listener!) If you are in doubt about (the stories) We have revealed to you (through Our Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), ask those who have been reading the Book (i.e. the Torah and the Gospel) before you. The truth has certainly come to you from your Lord; therefore, you should not be among the doubters."
  10,95,"And do not be among those who reject the revelations of Allah, for then you will be among the losers."
  10,96,"Indeed, those against whom the word of your Lord has proved true will not believe,"
  10,97,even if every sign were to come to them until they witness the painful punishment.
